        "body_4RJyFR": {
          "type": "body",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Named after the Finnish term for the Arctic Circle, Napapijri tracks its origins in the late 1980s in Aosta as a family-run, pioneering brand specialising in technical backpacks and bags designed for discerning travelers. Drawing inspiration from polar explorers, Napapijri utilised waxed cotton canvas, known for its durability and weather resistance. This choice of fabric set the tone for the brand's future in material research.</p>"
          }
        }
